George Vineyard derived in 1957 that in the harmonic approximation, the attempt frequency $
u_0 =  rac{\prod_{i=1}^{3N} 
u_i^{	ext{min}}}{\prod_{j=1}^{3N-1} 
u_j^{	ext{saddle}}}$ represents the ratio of partition function vibrational curvatures at the minimum vs the saddle point (where one imaginary mode along the reaction coordinate is removed).
